  "carriage_note": "Two operators may sign a receipt for the SAME submission_set: carriage is not exclusive, and a receipt says who carried it, never who alone may. The two same-set vectors below differ only in the signing key, so an implementation that keys receipts by submission_set_id alone collapses them and loses one operator's statement.",
  "must_hold": [
    "operator_id derives from the signing public key — a valid signature from an unrelated key must NOT pass as this operator",
    "the signed view is the receipt WITHOUT its signature field, canonicalized with JCS (sorted keys)",
    "two receipts over the same submission_set_id from different operators are both valid and distinct",
    "rules_version is carried, not assumed: the same operator signs under whichever domain the set closed in"
  ]
